482	    /// Gap 3: all-zero `0.0.0` base version bumped by Minor/Major. Plain
483	    /// (non-prerelease) releases go through the ordinary forward-bump branch,
484	    /// which has no zero-guard and behaves like any other release. The
485	    /// `patch == 0` / `minor == 0 && patch == 0` boundary guards only exist in
486	    /// the prerelease-finalization branch, so they are exercised here with an
487	    /// all-zero *prerelease* base (`0.0.0-alpha.0` / `0.0.0a1`), where the
488	    /// guard causes the bump to collapse back to the unchanged base `0.0.0`
489	    /// instead of advancing past it.
490	    #[test]
491	    fn semver_zero_base_plain_bump() {
